sion:**\n0\n\n', 'output': "Evaluation: Pocket 8s (8h, 8c) is a strong starting hand in heads-up poker, often ahead of the opponent's random range. However, as a medium pair, it is vulnerable to overcards appearing on the flop. Since you are currently in the lead for the game and deep-stacked, playing a lower-variance strategy is advantageous to protect your position.\n\nReason: Checking allows you to see the flop without inflating the pot size immediately. This controls the volatility of the hand, minimizing the risk of a large loss while still allowing you to hit a set or win at showdown with your pair if the board is favorable. Given that you have the option to Check (0), it is a prudent move to maintain your chip lead.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
