n the cumulative score, high-variance flips are generally unnecessary risks unless the edge is significant. A2s is not a dominant enough hand to risk the entire stack against a massive overbet unless I suspect the opponent is manic. A safe play preserves the lead.\n\nReason: While A2 suited is a decent starting hand, calling an immediate All-in (or near All-in) puts the entire stack at risk. Since I am currently in the lead cumulatively, folding and waiting for a better spot or a less expensive flop is the prudent strategy to maintain the advantage without taking a high-variance coin flip.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
